<h2>What is not here</h2>

<p>Coaching 101 and active listening as skills belong in a training module. A play can point to a module when a team lacks the skill, but it doesn't teach the skill itself. The distinction between discussion and dialogue is reference material that one play draws on.</p>

<h2>Open questions</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Do these plays depend on the enabling team's position (temporary, invited, aiming to leave)? If a play works just as well for any coach, it may belong in a general practitioner collection instead.</li>
  <li>Most likely source instances come from consultancy. External enablement has a commercial reason to stay engaged that internal enabling teams lack. Each instance should say which context it comes from.</li>
</ul>

